{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_09_observability_and_ops_structured_logging", "label": "Structured Logging (pino + ALS context + mandatory redaction)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/09-observability-and-ops.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Redaction paths live in one shared config rather than per-app copies; `fly logs` is ephemeral and never the system of record, so logs ship to Loki and a Tigris archive sink."}, {"id": "docs_09_observability_and_ops_opentelemetry", "label": "OpenTelemetry Tracing (W3C traceparent end-to-end)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/09-observability-and-ops.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "traceparent is stored in BullMQ job data so the worker resumes the trace \u2014 one trace covers 'user clicked Generate PDF \u2192 job \u2192 Playwright \u2192 Tigris'; voice sessions sample at 100% because volume is low and value per trace is high."}, {"id": "docs_09_observability_and_ops_alert_list", "label": "Alert List (page-worthy DB, queue, webhook, voice, OTP alerts)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/09-observability-and-ops.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_09_observability_and_ops_custom_metrics", "label": "Custom Prometheus Metrics (names are the contract)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/09-observability-and-ops.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_09_observability_and_ops_postgres_runbook", "label": "THE Postgres Runbook", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/09-observability-and-ops.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Fly deprecated unmanaged Postgres and the owner chose Fly-native anyway, so these mitigations are mandatory in-scope work rather than optional hardening \u2014 the custom image is ours to rebuild when Fly stops maintaining flex."}, {"id": "docs_09_observability_and_ops_backup_layers", "label": "Two Independent Backup Layers \u2192 Tigris", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/09-observability-and-ops.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The backup bucket is pinned to a different region from the database so a bom regional loss cannot take data and backups together; logical dumps survive anything that corrupts the physical timeline."}, {"id": "docs_09_observability_and_ops_restore_drill", "label": "Restore Drill (pre-launch gate + monthly, canary-row RPO proof)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/09-observability-and-ops.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A worker writes a timestamped canary row every minute, so now() \u2212 max(canary.at) on the restored DB is the empirically proven RPO rather than a stated intention."}, {"id": "docs_09_observability_and_ops_failover_procedure", "label": "Failover Procedure (fence first, never promote against a live primary)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/09-observability-and-ops.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Split-brain is the only unrecoverable state in the runbook; two nodes is a degraded state, not a stable one."}, {"id": "docs_09_observability_and_ops_disk_full_playbook", "label": "Disk-Full and OOM Playbooks", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/09-observability-and-ops.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Cause #1 is always WAL retention from stalled archiving or an inactive replication slot; dropping PowerSync's slot is a last resort because it forces a full resync of every field device."}, {"id": "docs_09_observability_and_ops_escape_hatch", "label": "Escape Hatch \u2014 logical replication to managed Postgres", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/09-observability-and-ops.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Triggered by two consecutive failed restore drills, an unexplained HA event, sustained bom capacity failures or ops load above ~2 person-days/month; plain Postgres end to end means nothing locks in."}, {"id": "docs_09_observability_and_ops_dr_targets", "label": "DR Targets (RPO \u22645 min, RTO \u22641 h) \u2014 stated then proven", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/09-observability-and-ops.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_09_observability_and_ops_deploys", "label": "Deploys (one Fly app per service, rolling, migrations as release_command)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/09-observability-and-ops.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every migration must be expand/contract compatible with the previous release because old machines serve traffic during the roll; with no feature flags, a bad merge rolls back rather than getting flagged off."}, {"id": "docs_09_observability_and_ops_secrets_rotation", "label": "Secrets Rotation Schedule (dual-accept windows)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/09-observability-and-ops.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_09_observability_and_ops_cost_monitoring", "label": "Cost Monitoring (fixed lines, sizing baseline, per-tenant COGS)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/09-observability-and-ops.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_09_observability_and_ops_structured_logging", "target": "docs_08_security_and_tenancy_secrets_management", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.75, "source_file": "docs/09-observability-and-ops.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_09_observability_and_ops_opentelemetry", "target": "docs_02_system_architecture_background_processing", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.85, "source_file": "docs/09-observability-and-ops.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_09_observability_and_ops_alert_list", "target": "docs_09_observability_and_ops_custom_metrics", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/09-observability-and-ops.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_09_observability_and_ops_alert_list", "target": "docs_06_offline_and_sync_powersync_deployment", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/09-observability-and-ops.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_09_observability_and_ops_alert_list", "target": "docs_07_integrations_compliancegate", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/09-observability-and-ops.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_09_observability_and_ops_postgres_runbook", "target": "docs_09_observability_and_ops_backup_layers", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/09-observability-and-ops.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_09_observability_and_ops_backup_layers", "target": "docs_09_observability_and_ops_restore_drill", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRA